## CSS Print Optimisation

## @media print

```css
@media print {
  /* Hide non-content elements */
  nav, footer, aside, .ads, .cookie-banner,
  button, video, audio { display: none !important; }

  /* Expand link URLs */
  a[href]::after { content: ' (' attr(href) ')'; }
  a[href^="#"]::after,
  a[href^="javascript:"]::after { content: ''; } /* skip internal/js links */

  /* Ensure readable text on white */
  body {
    color: #000;
    background: #fff;
    font-size: 12pt;
  }

  /* Use absolute units for print */
  .page { width: 100%; max-width: none; }
}
```

## Page Breaks

```css
@media print {
  h2, h3 { break-after: avoid; }   /* don't orphan a heading */
  figure  { break-inside: avoid; } /* keep image + caption together */
  section { break-before: page; }  /* start each section on new page */
}
```

## @page Rule

```css
@page {
  size: A4 portrait;
  margin: 2cm;
}

@page :first {
  margin-top: 4cm; /* extra top margin on first page */
}
```

## Practical Tips

- Load a separate print stylesheet via `<link rel="stylesheet" media="print">`.
- Test using Chrome DevTools → More tools → Rendering → Emulate CSS print media.
- Remove `background-color` from containers (ink saving) unless brand-critical.
- Set `max-width: none` on content wrappers to use full page width.

